            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the French for to honk, then the French for to mist up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: la pompe",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la pompe — \"the pump\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "La pompe numéro trois ne marche pas. Pump number three is not working."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "La pompe à essence is the petrol pump; une pompe à vélo is a bicycle pump."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of pompe is not settled. It is usually linked to Middle Low German pumpe 'pump' (EtymDB) and may imitate the sound of the pump."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
